-- title:
--   Regularity at the cusp ∞ of the pole chart, q=2
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 2$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carrying $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L((\mathsf q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) for level $q^2M'$ and the subgroup [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$, nonzero, have Laurent expansion the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Write $A_\infty =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgInf A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L144), the elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$. Let $\mathfrak n \subseteq A_\infty$ be a prime ideal consisting exactly of those $b$ whose Laurent expansion has $0$-th coefficient in the image of the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $B$ be a localisation of $A_\infty$ at $\mathfrak n$. Then $B$ is a regular local ring, $\dim B = 2$, the extension of $\mathfrak n$ to $B$ is generated by $\varpi$ and `jInvChartInf` (that is, $j^{-1}$), and $B/\varpi B$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the local regularity statement for the integral model of $X_H(q^2M')$ at the $\mathsf q$-adic cusp $\infty$ of the special fibre, in the case $q = 2$: the pole chart is regular of dimension two there, with $(\varpi, 1/j)$ a regular system of parameters and regular fibre over $A/\varpi$. It feeds the corresponding statement about regularity of the fibre used along the semistable-covering analysis of the modular curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_isRegularLocalRing_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_cuspInfty_xH_of_eq_two.lean

